      "side": 1,
      "message": "loadConfiguration() already logs Config error: {ERROR} before rethrowing (lines 161-165 of chassis_availability_monitor.cpp). discoverChassis() does the same.\n\nWithout the catch, an uncaught exception reaches std::terminate, which calls abort(). That produces SIGABRT and possibly a core dump. The daemon dies either way and the error is already in the journal.\n\nThe real differences are exit code 1 instead of SIGABRT, and no core dump. These are worth having, but the commit message should say so instead of implying a crash is being prevented.\n\nThe service has Restart\u003dalways. A persistently bad config will therefore restart in a loop with either exit path. Look at StartLimit* or RestartSec if that matters.\n\nThe message is now logged twice: \"Config error\" and then \"Failed to initialize chassis availability monitor\". This is harmless, but the second log line is redundant for config errors.\n\nThe catch also covers exceptions from bus.process_discard() and bus.wait(). The log text says \"Failed to initialize\", which is misleading for a runtime failure inside the loop.\n\nSuggestion: reword the log, for example \"Chassis availability monitor failed: {ERROR}\".\n\nMinor: the try follows constexpr auto configPath with no blank line. Style only.",
      "revId": "683cd06b5bc5199d50bf89780fc7720156aa0ae6",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
